Package: apch
Type: Package
Title: Adaptive Partial Conjunction Hypothesis for Subset-Level Inference
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
  person("Yuxin", "Li", email = "yuxin.li.gr@dartmouth.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
  person("Zicheng", "Lu", role = "aut"),
  person("Xiaolei", "Lin", email = "xiaoleilin@fudan.edu.cn", role = "aut")
 )
Description: Empirical Bayes inference for partial conjunction hypotheses
  across multiple features, such as traits or tissues. Each feature's
  effect-size distribution is modeled with an adaptive shrinkage prior, and
  the joint model learns how effect sizes are shared among jointly affected
  features. Reports subset-level local false discovery rates and local false
  sign rates with level-by-level subset selection, and allows correlated
  estimation errors across features.
